unted as covered. The actual line, toggle and branch percentages are pending the platform's coverage.read run on this testbench."}], "files": [{"path": "tick_timer_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "tick_timer_tb.sv: directed and scoreboard testbench for tick_timer", "summary": "Testbench for [requirement:req-33bb46282b], extending [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1]. It instantiates the approved [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1] with W=16.\n\n- Directed checks: exact expected register and irq values, derived cycle by cycle from the register map in the RTL header and its stated rules. Those rules are that a CTRL write takes the edge's place and that an expiry wins over a clear.\n- Scoreboard: a reference model checks rdata and irq at every negedge after reset release.\n- Verdict: prints the NIRMAAN-SIM line with the nonce plusarg, in the same form as the approved testbench.\n- Gate rules: it uses no $fopen, $system, DPI, include, Verilator config or coverage pragma.", "entry": "tick_timer_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The testbench is expected to pass on the approved RTL; this has not been run by me and is unverified.", "Expected uncoverable toggle points with W=16: rdata[31:16] and the constant unused_wdata wire; no other gaps are anticipated, but this is unmeasured.", "The coverage bounds of the requirement are not stated in the given sections, so whether the expected coverage meets them is unknown until coverage.read reports."], "escalation": null, "notes": "The testbench avoids driving one variable from several processes (separate directed and scoreboard counters) to stay clear of Verilator MULTIDRIVEN warnings. It assumes the gate builds with timing support, as the approved idle testbench already relies on # delays. Reset is released 1 ns after a clock edge to avoid the edge race present in the idle testbench. At most four 1 ns read delays follow any edge, so reads never cross the next posedge. The run-0001 evidence belongs to the upst